## What I Learned

### 1. Computer Components
| Component | Role | Analogy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| CPU | Processes instructions | The Brains |
| RAM | Short-term memory | Temporary, fast storage |
| Motherboard | Connects everything | Skeleton and Nerves |
| PSU | Provides power | Heart and Lungs |
| HDD/SSD | Long-term storage | Long-term Memory |
| GPU | Handles graphics | Visual Cortex |

### 2. Boot Sequence
The 5 steps a computer follows to start:
1. **Press Power Button** - Signal sent to PSU
2. **Firmware Starts** - UEFI/BIOS initializes hardware
3. **POST** - Power-On Self Test checks components
4. **Select Boot Device** - Finds where OS is stored
5. **Start Bootloader** - Loads the Operating System

## Key Takeaway
This room taught me the foundation of how hardware and software work together. Understanding boot process is important for troubleshooting and cybersecurity.

